dundant):**\n- Plan1: "X is the son of Y."\n- Plan2: "Y is the mother of X."\n- Plan3: "X\'s mother is Y."\n(These all verify the same relationship! Keep only ONE)\n\n**Examples of GOOD plans (independent):**\n- Plan1: "X is the son of Y." (verifies relationship)\n- Plan2: "Y\'s profession is acting." (new, independent information)\n(These verify different things)\n\n# Output Format\nplan1: [First independent statement]\nplan2: [Second independent statement]\n...\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Question: Who is the mother of the director of film Polish-Russian War (Film)?\n\nCurrent Memory (Already Known/Verified):\n\n\n## Task:\nBased on the Memory above, identify ALL independent, non-redundant pieces of information needed to answer the question.\n\n## Rules:\n1. DO NOT repeat information already in Memory\n2. Each plan should verify a DIFFERENT entity or relationship\n3. DO NOT generate multiple plans about the same thing (e.g., don\'t generate both "X is Y\'s son" and "Y is X\'s mother")\n4. Use specific names from Memory in your plans\n5. Each plan should be independently verifiable\n\nGenerate all necessary plans:\n'}]
